## #01 — Notes and preserve
Write notes first on NEW 06.09.md. Preserve source-before code/tests/docs under
evidence/identity05.06/before/, keeping old manifests and all review evidence.
Read 06.04/06.08. Do not change the store schema, delivery semantics, writer,
authentication claims, route authority or the completion witness guarantee.

## #02 — Inspection/2 returned identity
Change show --json's document schema to clerk-handoff-inspection/2 and add exactly
returned.event_sha256: SHA-256 of the exact returned-event bytes whose hash was
validated against the completion witness. Reuse the existing validated view's
event metadata; no second event reader in the consumer or added raw-file reread.
All other fields/checks/exit semantics remain as inspection/1. For queued/claimed
returned stays null. Corrupt/incomplete/unreadable metadata never supplies a usable
returned identity. For an intact historical event with a later changed artifact,
the digest stays the recorded event identity and the existing nonclean checks
remain; do not rehash the mutated artifact into a new return identity.
No optional claim digest and no extra fields/compatibility flags this slice.
Document inspection/1 as the predecessor with no event digest; existing source
snapshots remain preserved. There is no active adapter needing a hidden fallback.

## #03 — Diagnostic and consumer contract
Keep evidence single-line/nonblank. Distinguish empty/whitespace-only evidence
from nonblank evidence containing control characters; give a truthful refusal
message and preserve all no-write behavior. No new multiline convention.
README: exit0 means structurally valid projection; instructions:not-checked does
NOT mean verified or ready. A consumer needing usable instructions must pass
--instructions-base and require usable; a clean returned handoff also requires
state returned, completion/events/artifacts ok and no problems. State alone is
not enough. Observation/acknowledgement of a troubled record must retain its
attention diagnostics; do not hide it. This tool still cannot grant approval.
Retain CI-04 wording/semantics and its recorded rationale; no cosmetic overhaul.

## #04 — Verify the exact new contract
Run relocated original suite/demo, preserving before tests and explaining only
schema/field/diagnostic expectation changes. Add fresh-process tests comparing
event_sha256 to actual 0003 bytes AND the witness digest on clean return/replay;
queued/claimed null; damaged pair refuses; changed artifact retains event identity
but nonclean result; instruction base absent versus stale versus usable; blank
and control-containing evidence refuse without writes. Assert every inspection
leaves store bytes/names unchanged. Expected read failures yield valid JSON.
Do not claim symlink privileges if skipped. No broad fuzzing or repeated suites
without a change/failure. Keep source hashes and failed runs in new manifests.

Allowed writes: labs/clerk-handoff-pass02/, THIS batch/06.09 and new
evidence/identity05.06/. No other page/review, app, Prime-support, return capture,
pack assembly, kernel, queues, index/views, SoF or Observer branch changes.
No shared Git commits/pushes, network/model calls or activation. Prime publishes.
Fully reread code/tests/README, disposition notes, return HERE Did, Blocked, Need
with exact commands/results/hashes and one next bounded recommendation.

